      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T17:06:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thought on it a little more and did some experiments -- I don\u0027t think `__GENKSYMS__` is what I need. `struct gh_rm` is already not directly tracked by crc checker. I don\u0027t want ABI tools to track it because it is supposed to be an opaque pointer. This is opposite problem that vendor hooks have -- where they had the opaque pointer we wanted to not appear opaque in the ABI. As I understand from the docs [1], `__GENKSYMS__` is supposed to help maintain stability of the CRC, not remove definitions from the ABI.",
      "parentUuid": "4c6ef2c6_5948974b",
      "revId": "77493ff4423487d41ba00379ffd3ae5455312d1d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
